ng"}}, {"learning": {"0": "learning", "1": "learning"}}, {"By": {"0": "By", "1": "By"}}, {"doing": {"0": "doing", "1": "doing"}}, {"so": {"0": "so", "1": "so"}}, {"we": {"0": "we", "1": "we"}}, {"can": {"0": "can", "1": "can"}}, {"ensure": {"0": "ensure", "1": "ensure"}}, {"that": {"0": "that", "1": "that"}}, {"the": {"0": "the", "1": "the"}}, {"future": {"0": "future", "1": "future"}}, {"of": {"0": "of", "1": "of"}}, {"work": {"0": "work", "1": "work"}}, {"is": {"0": "is", "1": "is"}}, {"one": {"0": "one", "1": "one"}}, {"of": {"0": "of", "1": "of"}}, {"collaboration": {"0": "collaboration", "1": "collaboration"}}, {"between": {"0": "between", "1": "between"}}, {"humans": {"0": "humans", "1": "humans"}}, {"and": {"0": "and", "1": "and"}}, {"machines": {"0": "machines", "1": "machines"}}, {"rather": {"0": "rather", "1": "rather"}}, {"than": {"0": "than", "1": "than"}}, {"competition": {"0": "competition", "1": "competition"}}], "container": "The future of work is a topic that has been widely discussed in recent years, and one of the key factors shaping this future is automation. Automation refers to the use of technology to perform tasks that were previously carried out by humans. While automation offers numerous benefits such as increased efficiency and productivity, there is also concern about the potential displacement of human workers. Advances in technology, particularly in the field of artificial intelligence and robotics, have led to the automation of various tasks across industries. Jobs that were once performed by humans, such as data entry, manufacturing, and even customer service, are now being done by machines. This shift has resulted in fears that automation will lead to widespread job loss and unemployment. It is true that in some cases, automation has led to job displacement. For example, the rise of self-checkout machines in supermarkets has reduced the need for human cashiers. Similarly, the use of automated systems in manufacturing has decreased the demand for manual labor. However, it is important to note that automation also creates new job opportunities. As technology advances, new roles in fields such as software development, data analysis, and artificial intelligence programming are emerging. While it is difficult to predict the exact impact of automation on the labor market, studies have shown that it is likely to lead to a transformation of jobs rather than complete obsolescence. This means that while some jobs may be eliminated, new jobs will be created, often requiring a different set of skills. For example, as machines take over repetitive and mundane tasks, workers will have the opportunity to focus on more complex and creative tasks that require human judgement and critical thinking. To prepare for the future of work, it is important for individuals to acquire skills that are less susceptible to automation. This includes skills such as problem-solving, adaptability, creativity, and emotional intelligence, which are difficult for machines to replicate. Additionally, lifelong learning and upskilling will become increasingly important as technology continues to advance. In conclusion, automation will undoubtedly shape the future of work. While there may be concerns about job displacement, it is important to recognize that automation also brings new opportunities. The key lies in adapting to the changing landscape by acquiring skills that are less susceptible to automation and embracing lifelong learning. By doing so, we can ensure that the future of work is one of collaboration between humans and machines, rather than competition.", "encoded_message": "The tomorrow of labor is a subject that has been largely talked about in latest years, and one of the central influences influencing this future is automation. Robotization relates to the application of technology to execute functions that were prior conducted out by individuals. While automation delivers many gains such including enhanced efficiency a